87
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
New parents do tend to get confused

88
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
and the notion that scout camping

89
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
is anything like the parent and son camping

90
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
they did in Cub Scouts

91
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
really kind of needs to be erased as soon as possible.

92
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Most parents do relate well

93
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
to the concept of sports team organization and dynamics.

94
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
It's something they can understand.

95
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
There is a difference, though,

96
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
in that coaches in sports teams

97
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
usually have a lot more control over what happens.

98
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
They run the drills, they call the place,

99
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
select players and things like that.

100
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
and in scouting and a scout master's job

101
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
is really quite different.

102
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
He helps those processes

103
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
but he's only mentoring the team captain

104
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
or the senior patrol leader

105
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
and he's not really directly involved

106
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
in calling the shots while the game is being played.

107
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
It's kind of difficult for an adult scout leader,

108
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
especially one with coaching experience,

109
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
to realize and embrace the difference

110
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
between sports and scouting. in that regard,

111
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Of course, training is important,

112
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
and boy scout leader fast start training

113
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
and the scout master specific training

114
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
gives everyone a better understanding

115
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
of scouting as a whole,

116
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
The differences between Cub Scouts

117
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
and Boy Scouts and the role of adults in a troop.

118
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
And once we're trained

119
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
